# Anthropic kill switch (pf anchor: com.apple/250.AnthropicKillSwitch)
# Traffic to Anthropic may only leave through the corporate VPN (ipsec0, Chile).
# If the VPN is down, packets to Anthropic are rejected instead of leaving
# through the real connection, so Claude never sees the real IP.
# Source: Anthropic AS399358 (IPv4) + 2607:6bc0::/48 (IPv6).

table <anthropic> const persist { \
	160.79.104.0/23, 160.79.106.0/24, 209.249.57.0/24, \
	38.46.212.0/24, 38.84.152.0/24, 2607:6bc0::/48 }

pass  out quick on ipsec0 to <anthropic> keep state
block return out quick to <anthropic>
